ymbol}\" — no unit_id/footnote_markers mentioned for config. Rule 5: \"Values follow the same structured form: {condition, value, unit_symbol}.\" So config values just need condition, value, unit_symbol. Good — I'll use those three keys only for config_level. For type_level and model_level, the full shape {value, unit_symbol, unit_id, footnote_markers}. For model_level values: {model, value, footnote_markers?} — the example shows {\"model\": \"Emax=25t\", \"value\": 25} without unit at value level (unit at attribute level). Good — model_level values: {model, value}.\n\nOK, writing final JSON now.\n\nOne more consideration: \"scheme\": is \"B\" correct for OIML Basic Certificate? Yes — OIML-CS Scheme B is \"Basic Certificate of Conformity\". Confident.\n\nEdition: 2013 as integer.\n\nLet me write the JSON.\n\nAlso description should mention sealing/passwords? Keep moderate.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-CZ-16.04\",\n    \"scheme\": \"B\",\n    \"page_total\": 8,\n    \"member_state\": \"Czech Republic\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2017-10-12\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"Czech Metrology Institute\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Okružní 31\", \"638 00 Brno\", \"CZ\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"Jan Kalandra\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Arkon Flow Systems, s.r.o.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Berkova 534/92\", \"612 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Arkon Flow Systems, s.r.o.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Berkova 534/92\", \"612 00 Brno\", \"Czech Republic\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MAGX2\"],\n    \"module_designation\": null,\n    \"description\": \"...\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {...},\n  \"characteristics\": {...},\n  \"matrix_tables\": [...],\n  \"recommendation\": {...},\n  \"test_reports\": [...],\n  \"revision_history\": [{\"revision\": \"1\", \"date\": null, \"changes\": null}]\n}\n\nLet me write the description:\n\n\"Electromagnetic water meter for metering cold and hot potable water, based on an inductive principle, with PTFE and hard rubber lining, straight inlet (5 × diameter) and outlet (3 × diameter) length, without flow conditioner, equipped with an electronic calculating/indicating device. Two modifications: compact and remote version (maximum cable length for remote version 6 m). The display shows volume (positive, negative, total and auxiliary) in m³ and flow rate in m³/h; the meter is not designed to measure reverse flow. Access to metrological parameters is secured by user, service and factory passwords; software version and checksum can be displayed using buttons. Optional frequency output for remote reading or RS 485 communication. Nominal diameters DN25 to DN300 with flanged connections; horizontal and vertical mounting (flow axis) allowed, indicating device at top or side.\"\n\nNow write model_level.\n\n\"model_level\": [\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"nominal_diameter\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN25\", \"value\": 25},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN32\", \"value\": 32},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN40\", \"value\": 40},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN50\", \"value\": 50},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN65\", \"value\": 65},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN80\", \"value\": 80},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN100\", \"value\": 100},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN125\", \"value\": 125},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN150\", \"value\": 150},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN200\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN250\", \"value\": 250},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN300\", \"value\": 300}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"permanent_flowrate_q3\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN25\", \"value\": 16.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN32\", \"value\": 25.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN40\", \"value\": 40.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN50\", \"value\": 63.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN65\", \"value\": 100.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN80\", \"value\": 160.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN100\", \"value\": 250.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN125\", \"value\": 400.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN150\", \"value\": 630.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN200\", \"value\": 1000.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN250\", \"value\": 1000.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN300\", \"value\": 1600.0}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"overload_flowrate_q4\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"m³/h\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN25\", \"value\": 20.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN32\", \"value\": 31.3},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN40\", \"value\": 50.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN50\", \"value\": 78.8},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN65\", \"value\": 125.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN80\", \"value\": 200.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN100\", \"value\": 312.5},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN125\", \"value\": 500.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN150\", \"value\": 787.5},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN200\", \"value\": 1250.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN250\", \"value\": 1250.0},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN300\", \"value\": 2000.0}\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"attribute\": \"length_of_horizontal_water_meter\",\n    \"unit_symbol\": \"mm\",\n    \"values\": [\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN25\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN32\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN40\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN50\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN65\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN80\", \"value\": 200},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN100\", \"value\": 250},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN125\", \"value\": 250},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN150\", \"value\": 300},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN200\", \"value\": 350},\n      {\"model\": \"MAGX2 DN250\", \"value\": 400},\n      {\"model\